  {
   "topic": "Reverse bias",
   "page": 20,
   "text": "Only forward operation within the current rating is intended. Continuous reverse voltage, or forward voltage held below the emission threshold, risks migration in the die, with changed characteristics or damage as the result."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Binning and test pulses",
   "page": 20,
   "text": "Brightness and wavelength are sorted with 25 ms current pulses (intensity tolerance ±11 %, wavelength ±1 nm); forward voltage with 1 ms pulses (±0.1 V)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Thermal",
   "page": 20,
   "text": "Junction-to-ambient resistance of 900 K/W max applies with the part on FR4 and at least 5 mm² of pad on each terminal; junction-to-solder-point resistance is 510 K/W max. Both are 6σ limits. Continuous current derates linearly from 25 mA to 5 mA between 35 °C and 85 °C ambient, or between 60 °C and 85 °C at the solder point."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Typical curves",
   "page": 20,
   "text": "Curves and typical figures are statistical and need not match any single device. Where a curve is drawn broken (the high-current end of relative intensity against forward current), device-to-device spread within one packing unit is larger."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Soldering and cleaning",
   "page": 11,
   "text": "Reflow under a nitrogen atmosphere gives the best joints. Ultrasonic cleaning is not allowed for this package. Moisture sensitivity is MSL 2 to JEDEC J-STD-020E; parts ship dry-packed with desiccant and a humidity indicator card to JEDEC J-STD-033."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Corrosion",
   "page": 18,
   "text": "The device holds silver-bearing filled materials, which aggressive atmospheres can attack, so exposure to corrosive substances in storage, assembly and use is to be kept low. It meets corrosion robustness class 3B: 14 days at 40 °C, 90 % RH and 15 ppm H2S. Parts that discoloured in that test stayed inside their failure limits (IEC 60810)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Eye safety",
   "page": 18,
   "text": "Assessed to IEC 62471:2006, the device is in the exempt risk group for a 10000 s exposure. Like any bright source it can still dazzle and leave afterimages."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Package",
   "page": 10,
   "text": "The die sits on a 0.3 mm board substrate under a colourless diffused resin body, offset toward the cathode end; each end carries a half-round notch (R0.2). Dimensions are in mm with a ±0.1 mm tolerance unless one is given."
  }
